 "tier": null,
 "title": "Solving One Step Equations",
 "summary": "Learn how to undo one operation to find a missing number or letter in a simple equation.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "An equation tells us that two things are equal.  \nTo solve an equation we need to find out what a missing number is."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Here is an equation:"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "a + 9 = 15"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "a is a missing number. To solve this equation we need to work out what number a is."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Because both sides of the equation are equal if we do the same thing to both sides the equation will still be equal."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "At the moment we have 9 added onto a. To get a by itself we can do the opposite of adding 9, subtracting 9. If we subtract 9 from both sides of the equation we have:"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "a + 9 - 9 = 15 - 9  \na = 6"
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
