  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "We have solved the equation and found that a = 6"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 1: Solve: b - 12 = 8",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We can add 12 to both sides of the equation to get b by itself\n\nb - 12 + 12 = 8 + 12  \nb = 20",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 2: Solve: 5c = 45",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "5c means 5 × c  \nThe opposite of multiplying by 5 is dividing by 5  \nTo get c by itself we can divide both sides by 5.\n\n5c⁄5 = 45⁄5  \nc = 9",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 3: Solve: d⁄3 = 12",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "5c means 5 × c  \nThe opposite of dividing by by 3 is multiplying by 3  \nTo get d by itself we can multiply both sides by 3.\n\n3d⁄3 = 12 × 3  \nd = 36",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
